(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "2607241900"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141 -- pilot: layer a governed ToSMonitor-LLM / ToSArchiveGovernor actor on top of ONE existing lei-* archive repo, scoped to that single repo only"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-24"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607199960-cloud-itonami-lei-top10-universe-expansion.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607241800-cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger-actor-blueprint.edn" "cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141/docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md")), (:adr/repo-touched "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141"), (:adr/pattern "sealed ToSMonitor-LLM advisor + independent ToSArchiveGovernor + append-only audit ledger, modeled directly on cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger's Store/Registry/Advisor/Governor/Phase/Operation/Sim shape (2607241800), which itself follows cloud-itonami-isic-6492/6493; registered at :implemented for this one repo only"), (:adr/scope-is-one-repo-only "this ADR does NOT change ADR-2607110300's design for the other ~154 cloud-itonami-lei-* archive repos, which remain plain read-only archives, exactly as ADR-2607110300 specifies (independent third-party archive, not a governed Advisor/Governor actor). Only cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141 (The Procter & Gamble Company) gains an actor layer, as an explicit, owner-approved pilot to test whether the pattern is worth extending further"), (:adr/why-pilot-not-fleet-wide "owner explicitly chose a 1-2 repo pilot over a fleet-wide rollout when asked (2026-07-24 session): scale (roughly 155 archive repos today, ADR-2607199960's own target is tens of thousands), cost (one governed actor here is ~1200 lines of source+tests versus a ~15-line archive), and the fact that ADR-2607110300 deliberately chose the archive-only shape for this family all argue for proving the pattern on one entity before deciding whether to extend it, rather than retrofitting the whole family in one sweep"), (:adr/archive-layer-untouched "blueprint.edn, README.md (updated only to describe the new actor layer honestly, not to change the archive claims), NOTICE, and 80-data/public/tos.journal.edn are UNCHANGED in shape and meaning by this ADR -- tos.journal.edn stays the archive-of-record exactly as ADR-2607110300 defines it (a quad-log EDN, entity-id/attr/value/tx/op tuples), and the new actor NEVER writes to it. The actor's own append-only ledger is a separate in-process/Datomic structure (commitledger-style MemStore|DatomicStore), not a new top-level archive file, so a future automated re-fetch/archivist pipeline can adopt or ignore this actor's proposals without any migration of the existing archive format"), (:adr/single-actuation-tos-change-proposal "one actuation, :tos/change-proposal (stake :actuation/archive-update, always set regardless of :material-change?), permanently excluded from every phase's :auto set -- matching cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger's own :commitment/record/:commitment/tranche-release exclusion exactly (not conditionally). Updating the public record of what a company's legal terms say is treated with the same never-autonomous discipline commitledger applies to its two money-adjacent actuations, even though this actor moves no money at all: EVERY :tos/change-proposal run, material or not, always escalates to a human archivist at every phase 0-3. This pilot deliberately does not implement an auto-eligible 'routine reconfirmation, no change detected' path -- a single, simple, always-escalate actuation is judged the right scope for a first pilot proving the governed-actor pattern itself, not the phase-3 autonomy ladder; that refinement is left to a follow-up"), (:adr/six-hard-checks "grounding-violations (every quoted excerpt in the proposal's :cites must be an exact substring of the candidate full-text -- no hallucinated quotes, the core anti-fabrication check for this domain), provenance-incomplete-violations (candidate must carry non-blank source-url/retrieved-at/sha256/full-text), sha256-mismatch-violations (ground-truth recompute of the candidate's own sha256, ANY mismatch against the advisor-echoed value is HARD -- ADR-2607110300's own provenance discipline enforced structurally, not just by convention), retrieved-at-not-advancing-violations (candidate retrieved-at must be >= the archived baseline's retrieved-at -- refuses to propose a change from stale/out-of-order input), doc-type-unknown-violations (candidate doc-type must be a member of a known enum, matching the archive's own :tos/doc-type vocabulary), source-domain-mismatch-violations (candidate source-url's domain must match the company's own blueprint.edn website domain, independently re-verified from the store's own company record, never the advisor's self-report -- this actor's own DISTINCTIVE check, guarding the exact 'independent third-party archive could misattribute a document to the wrong company' risk that is specific to this LEI-keyed archive family)"), (:adr/mock-advisor-only-in-pilot "clojure -M:dev:run and the default test suite always use the deterministic mock-advisor (offline, no network calls), matching every prior actor in this fleet; commitledger.advisor-style llm-advisor/kotoba-server-CACAO wiring is written as a swappable seam (per the injection-boundary convention) but is NOT invoked live anywhere in this pilot -- no live fetch of a company's current ToS page and no live kotobase.net publish happen as part of landing this ADR"), (:adr/test-status-tos-monitor "governor contract (one test per HARD check, 6 total, plus the high-stakes/never-auto invariant), phase invariants (0-3, material-change permanently excluded from every :auto set), store parity (MemStore vs DatomicStore via langchain-store's ls/enc/ls/dec*, ADR-2607141600), advisor smoke; 25 tests / 70 assertions, all passing; clj-kondo: 0 errors (2 harmless warnings from cross-platform :cljs-branch analysis of the :clj-only sha256 recompute helper, documented in tosmonitor.registry's own ns docstring, do not fail --fail-level error)"), (:adr/west-registration "this repo (cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141) is ALREADY a registered west project (manifest/west.yml), unlike a from-scratch new-actor registration -- no new manifest/repos.edn or west.yml entry is needed for this ADR; only the repo's own content changes on a feature branch + PR, merged into the repo's own main"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607241900: pilot -- ToSMonitor-LLM / ToSArchiveGovernor on cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141 only\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: ADR-2607110300 (the archive-only design this ADR does NOT change for\n  the other ~154 repos); ADR-2607199960 (top-10/universe expansion of the same\n  archive family -- unaffected); ADR-2607241800 (`cloud-itonami-commitment-\n  ledger`, the actor this pilot's Store/Registry/Advisor/Governor/Phase/\n  Operation/Sim shape is modeled directly on); `cloud-itonami-lei-\n  2572ibtt8cczw6au4141/docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md` (repo-local\n  architecture record).\n\n## Context\n\nA prior session in this superproject asked what the current maturity and\ncoverage of the `cloud-itonami-lei-*` family is. The honest answer (recorded\nseparately, not in this ADR): ~155 repos exist, and every one of them is a\nplain archive -- `blueprint.edn` + `LICENSE`/`NOTICE`/`README.md` +\n`80-data/public/tos.journal.edn`, with no `src/`, no Governor, no StateGraph,\nno tests. ADR-2607110300 intentionally designed them this way (`independent\nthird-party archive... not a governed Advisor/Governor actor`), and every\nrepo's own README says so explicitly.\n\nThe owner then asked to improve this family's maturity. Given a direct choice\nbetween (a) automating the intake pipeline, (b) upgrading `lei-*` repos into\ngoverned actors matching this workspace's `build-actor` pattern, or (c)\nsimply growing the coverage numbers, the owner chose (b) -- and, when asked\nabout scope, explicitly chose a 1-2 repo PILOT over a fleet-wide rewrite of\nall ~155 repos.\n\nThis matters because ADR-2607110300's archive-only shape was a deliberate\ndesign decision, not an oversight -- converting the whole family into actors\nwithout owner sign-off would have silently reversed an accepted ADR at scale.\nA pilot, by contrast, tests the pattern on one entity without touching\nADR-2607110300's standing design for the rest of the family.\n\nWhile researching how to build this, this session discovered that\n`cloud-itonami`'s own actor fleet (the `cloud-itonami-isic-*`/`cloud-itonami-\ncommitment-ledger` family, ~190+ repos, a COMPLETELY SEPARATE set from\n`cloud-itonami-lei-*`) already has a mature, actively-used governed-actor\npattern -- most recently `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger` (ADR-2607241800,\nregistered the SAME DAY as this ADR). That pattern (Store/Registry/Advisor/\nGovernor/Phase/Operation/Sim `.cljc` modules, langgraph-clj StateGraph,\nlangchain-store-backed Datomic parity, mock-advisor-by-default, phase 0-3\nrollout, HARD/soft check split) is what this pilot follows directly, rather\nthan re-deriving the older `gftd-talent-actor`/`robotaxi-actor` template from\nfirst principles -- it is the SAME underlying `build-actor` skill pattern,\njust the freshest and most battle-tested instance of it in this workspace.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Scope: exactly one repo.** Only `cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141`\n   (The Procter & Gamble Company, the entity this session had already sampled\n   while assessing fleet maturity) gains an actor layer. The other ~154\n   `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repos are untouched by this ADR and remain governed\n   solely by ADR-2607110300. Extending this pattern further is an explicit\n   FOLLOW-UP decision, not implied by this ADR.\n2. **ToSMonitor-LLM (sealed) (- ToSArchiveGovernor (independent).** New\n   `tosmonitor.*` namespaces (`src/tosmonitor/{store,registry,advisor,\n   governor,phase,operation,sim}.cljc`), modeled directly on `commitledger.*`\n   (ADR-2607241800): `tosmonitor.store` (MemStore | DatomicStore via\n   `langchain-store.core`'s `ls/enc`/`ls/dec*`, ADR-2607141600),\n   `tosmonitor.registry` (ground-truth SHA-256 recompute + candidate/baseline\n   shape helpers + the pure `fold-quad-log` bridge to the archive's own\n   quad-log EDN format), `tosmonitor.advisor` (mock-advisor default;\n   llm-advisor written as a swap, never invoked live in this pilot),\n   `tosmonitor.governor` (the six HARD checks below), `tosmonitor.phase`\n   (0-3 rollout), `tosmonitor.operation` (langgraph-clj StateGraph, one\n   actuation `:tos/change-proposal`), `tosmonitor.sim` (offline demo).\n3. **The archive-of-record is never touched.** `80-data/public/\n   tos.journal.edn` keeps its existing quad-log shape and meaning exactly as\n   ADR-2607110300 established it; this actor's `commit-record!` writes ONLY\n   to its own append-only ledger/draft-history structure (an in-process\n   MemStore atom or a Datomic-backed store, never a new top-level archive\n   file). A future human archivist or automated re-fetch pipeline can adopt\n   this actor's `:material-change?` proposals into the real archive, or\n   ignore them, without any migration of the existing archive format.\n4. **Single actuation, `:tos/change-proposal`, stake `:actuation/\n   archive-update` (always set, material or not).** PERMANENTLY excluded\n   from every phase's `:auto` set, unconditionally -- mirroring\n   `commitledger.phase`'s own `:commitment/record`/`:commitment/tranche-\n   release` exclusion exactly, not merely when the proposal happens to be\n   material. A human archivist always signs off before this actor's verdict\n   on a candidate is recorded, whether or not it detected a change. This\n   pilot deliberately ships a single, always-escalate actuation rather than\n   also building an auto-eligible 'routine, no change detected'\n   reconfirmation path -- proving the governed-actor SHAPE (Store/\n   Registry/Advisor/Governor/Phase/Operation/Sim, six independently\n   re-verified HARD checks, append-only ledger) is this pilot's goal; a\n   lower-stakes auto-eligible op is a natural, explicitly out-of-scope\n   follow-up once the pattern itself is validated.\n5. **Six HARD governor checks**, every one independently re-verified from\n   the request's own candidate data and the store's own baseline/company\n   record, never taken on the advisor's self-report alone (this fleet's\n   standing convention):\n   - `grounding-violations` -- every excerpt string in the proposal's\n     `:cites` must be an exact substring of the candidate's own full text.\n     No hallucinated quotes. The core anti-fabrication check for this\n     domain.\n   - `provenance-incomplete-violations` -- candidate must carry non-blank\n     `:source-url`/`:retrieved-at`/`:sha256`/`:full-text`.\n   - `sha256-mismatch-violations` -- ground-truth recompute\n     (`tosmonitor.registry/sha256-hex`) of the candidate's own full text;\n     any mismatch against the value carried on the candidate is HARD.\n     Enforces ADR-2607110300's own provenance discipline structurally, not\n     merely by convention. Honest V1 scope: recompute is `:clj`-only\n     (`java.security.MessageDigest`, synchronous); a `:cljs` build falls\n     back to trusting the candidate-supplied hash, since the Web Crypto\n     digest API is Promise-based and cannot be called from a synchronous\n     governor check -- documented, not silently assumed, matching this\n     fleet's honest-scope-boundary convention (e.g. commitledger's\n     JPN-only rate-ceiling tiers, no-live-HTTP self-registration check).\n   - `retrieved-at-not-advancing-violations` -- candidate `:retrieved-at`\n     must be `>=` the archived baseline's `:retrieved-at`. Refuses to\n     propose a change from stale/out-of-order input.\n   - `doc-type-unknown-violations` -- candidate `:doc-type` must be a member\n     of a known enum matching the archive's own `:tos/doc-type` vocabulary.\n   - `source-domain-mismatch-violations` -- candidate `:source-url`'s domain\n     must match the company's own `blueprint.edn` website domain,\n     independently re-verified from the store's own company record. This\n     actor's own DISTINCTIVE check (per this fleet's convention that every\n     actor's ADR names its own novel contribution) -- it guards the risk\n     specific to an LEI-keyed independent-archive family: misattributing a\n     document to the wrong company.\n6. **Mock-advisor only in this pilot.** `clojure -M:dev:run` and the test\n   suite always exercise the deterministic `mock-advisor`; no live fetch of\n   a company's current ToS page and no live `kotoba-server`/CACAO publish\n   happen anywhere in landing this ADR. `llm-advisor` exists as a written,\n   swappable seam (the same injection-boundary convention every actor in\n   this fleet follows) but is not invoked.\n7. **No new west/manifest registration needed.** Unlike a from-scratch new\n   actor repo, `cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141` is already a\n   registered west project. This ADR changes only that repo's own content,\n   on a feature branch, merged via PR into that repo's own `main`.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) Directly answers the maturity question this session started from: one\n  real, tested, governed actor now exists in the `cloud-itonami-lei-*`\n  family, proving the `build-actor` pattern is applicable here without\n  guessing.\n- (+) ADR-2607110300's design for the other ~154 archive repos is completely\n  unaffected -- this is additive to one repo, not a silent fleet-wide policy\n  reversal.\n- (+) The archive-of-record (`tos.journal.edn`) keeps its exact existing\n  shape; nothing about ADR-2607110300's provenance/quad-log discipline needs\n  to change for this actor to exist alongside it.\n- (+) Reuses a proven, same-day template (`cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger`)\n  rather than inventing a new actor shape, keeping this fleet's actors\n  structurally consistent.\n- (-) Only 1 of ~155 repos gains this layer; the coverage question (\"how\n  many `lei-*` repos are governed actors\") is still effectively 0% until a\n  follow-up decision extends this pattern, which this ADR deliberately does\n  not pre-commit to.\n- (-) `sha256-mismatch-violations`'s ground-truth recompute is JVM-only in\n  V1; a `:cljs` build of this actor trusts the candidate-supplied hash for\n  that one check, an honest but real gap until a portable digest is added.\n- (-) No live integration: this pilot never actually re-fetches a company's\n  current ToS page over the network, so it cannot yet detect a real-world\n  change on its own -- a human or a future scheduled job must still supply\n  the `:candidate` input.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Option | Verdict | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| Automate the intake pipeline instead (bulk discovery) | (rejected for this decision) | Owner explicitly chose the actor-upgrade path when asked directly |\n| Convert all ~155 `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repos to actors now | (rejected) | Owner explicitly chose a 1-2 repo pilot; a fleet-wide rewrite would silently reverse ADR-2607110300's archive-only design without proving the pattern first |\n| Design a new actor shape from first principles (`gftd-talent-actor` template) | (rejected) | `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger` (2607241800) is a same-org, same-day, more mature instance of the identical `build-actor` pattern; following it directly keeps this fleet structurally consistent |\n| Have the actor write directly into `tos.journal.edn` | (rejected) | Would conflate a governed actor's DRAFT proposals with the archive-of-record ADR-2607110300 defines; a separate append-only ledger keeps the archive format and this actor's proposals independently evolvable |\n| Wire a live ToS re-fetch + kotoba-server publish into this pilot | (deferred) | Out of scope for proving the actor pattern itself; adding live network calls to a first pilot increases blast radius for no additional signal about whether the governed-actor SHAPE is right |\n| Two actuations (change-proposal + archive-write), mirroring commitledger's two-actuation shape | (rejected) | This domain has only one real decision point (propose a change); a second actuation would be manufactured complexity with no analog to commitledger's genuinely separate record/tranche-release events |\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607110300 (`90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn`)\n- ADR-2607199960 (`90-docs/adr/2607199960-cloud-itonami-lei-top10-universe-expansion.edn`)\n- ADR-2607241800 (`90-docs/adr/2607241800-cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger-actor-blueprint.edn`)\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger` (the direct template)\n- `cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141/docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md`\n- https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141\n")))
